(Evaluating the Impact of ChatGPT on Information Retrieval and Academic Study) Tj T*
(Authors: Nguyen, T. H., Tran, M. Q., & Le, V. K. \(2024\)) Tj T*
(Journal: Computers and Education: Artificial Intelligence, 6\(1\), 100215.) Tj T*
(DOI: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.caeai.2024.100215) Tj T*
(---------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj T*
(ABSTRACT:) Tj T*
(This study investigates how undergraduate students adopt ChatGPT for academic) Tj T*
(literature search, concept summarization, and research drafting across 4 universities.) Tj T*
(Sample size: N = 420 undergraduate students \(experimental group n = 210, control n = 210\).) Tj T*
(---------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj T*
(KEY EMPIRICAL FINDINGS:) Tj T*
(1. Literature Search Efficiency: Students using ChatGPT increased their literature) Tj T*
(   retrieval speed by 35% compared to traditional keyword search \(p < 0.001\).) Tj T*
(2. Comprehension Score: Concept outlining accuracy improved by 18.5% when students) Tj T*
(   combined AI prompts with manual syllabus verification.) Tj T*
(3. Hallucination Risk: 28.0% of unverified AI-generated citations contained fabricated) Tj T*
(   DOIs or inaccurate publication years, requiring strict human fact-checking.) Tj T*
